    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 26,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 26,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "While the styles may differ between platforms, the core building blocks are the same. Modern cross-platform frameworks like Ionic provide pre-built, customizable UI components that automatically adapt their look and feel to each platform."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 28,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 28,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Using a single set of UI components across iOS, Android and web apps enables massive code reuse. Developers only need to build features once and can tweak styling as needed for each platform."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 30,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 30,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Web-Based vs Native Cross-Platform Approaches"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 32,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 32,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "There are two main approaches to cross-platform development: web-based and native."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 34,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 34,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Web-based frameworks like Ionic use standard web technologies like HTML, CSS and JavaScript. The UI runs in a web view, with plugins providing access to native device features. While performance was a concern in the past, modern JavaScript engines have mostly closed the gap with native."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 36,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 36,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Native cross-platform frameworks like React Native and Flutter take a different approach. They provide React or Dart code that gets compiled to native widgets and code. This enables closer to native performance but requires using proprietary languages and tools."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 38,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 38,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Ultimately, the choice depends on your team's skills and goals. Web-based frameworks enable you to leverage existing web talent. Native frameworks require more specialized skills but may have performance benefits for demanding apps."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 40,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 40,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Supercharging Development Speed With Ionic"
        }
      ]
    },
